{"id":8189427,"docketId":65287177,"caseName":"Allison v. Texas","caseNameFull":"Allison v. Texas","slug":"allison-v-texas","docketNumber":"No. 704","dateFiled":"1935-05-13","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1935,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Mr. Clarence E. Farmer, with whom Mr. G. R. Lipscomb was on the brief, for appellant. Mr. William McCraw, Attorney General of Texas, Mr. Will R. Parker, District Attorney, Messrs. Cecil C. Rotsch and Homer B. Green, Assistant District Attorneys, and Mr. Lloyd W. Davidson, State's Attorney, were on the brief for appellee.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":0,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8151358,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":2309,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"AAiK\">\n\n<em>Per Curiam:</em>\n</author>\n<p id=\"AzF\">The appeal herein is dismissed (1) for the reason that the judgment of the state court sought to be reviewed is based upon a non-federal ground adequate to support it, <em>Stone </em>v. <em>State, </em>48 Tex. Cr. 114; <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"3920072\"><a href=\"/opinion/4154968/stone-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Stone v. State\">86 S. W. 1029</a></span>; <em>Farson Son </em>&amp; <em>Co. </em>v. <em>Bird, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"99249\"><a href=\"/opinion/99249/farson-son-co-v-bird/#271\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Farson, Son &amp; Co. v. Bird\">248 U. S. 268, 271</a></span>; <em>Doyle </em>v. <em>Atwell, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"100184\"><a href=\"/opinion/100184/new-york-ex-rel-doyle-v-atwell/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: New York Ex Rel. Doyle v. Atwell\">261 U. S. 590</a></span>, <em>McCoy </em>v. <em>Shaw, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"101309\"><a href=\"/opinion/101309/mccoy-v-shaw/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: McCoy v. Shaw\">277 U. S. 302</a></span>, and (2) for the want of a substantial federal question, <em>Watson </em>v. <em>Maryland, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"97286\"><a href=\"/opinion/97286/watson-v-maryland/#175\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Watson v. Maryland\">218 U. S. 173, 175-180</a></span>; <em>Crane </em>v. <em>Johnson, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98834\"><a href=\"/opinion/98834/crane-v-johnson/#342\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Crane v. Johnson\">242 U. S. 339, 342-344</a></span>; <em>McNaughton </em>v. <em>Johnson, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"98835\"><a href=\"/opinion/98835/mcnaughton-v-johnson/#348\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: McNaughton v. Johnson\">242 U. S. 344, 348-349</a></span>; <em>Graves </em>v. <em>Minnesota, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"100937\"><a href=\"/opinion/100937/graves-v-minnesota/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Graves v. Minnesota\">272 U. S. 425</a></span>; <em>Hurwitz </em>v. <em>North, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"100845\"><a href=\"/opinion/100845/missouri-ex-rel-hurwitz-v-north/#43\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Missouri Ex Rel. Hurwitz v. North\">271 U. S. 40, 43</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}